The standard deviation (i.e., the standard error) of the sampling distribution of the mean under the null hypothesis is  

\[
\sigma_{\bar{x}}=\frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
   =\frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
   \approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
   \approx 0.22 .
\]

So the standard deviation of the null‑hypothesis test statistic is about **0.22**.
